PROPOSED — NOT APPLIED. Task 6, gated on Easton's explicit go-ahead.

Scope note on the brief's proposal
----------------------------------
The brief proposes recording "actual fill price and fill timestamp". Both are
already captured today: price_monitor passes `current_price` into
_close_position, which stores it as `Trade.price`, and the SELL row's
`opened_at`/`closed_at` are set at fill time. Adding those two columns would
be near-redundant and would not close Pattern C.

Pattern C is a *series* mismatch, not a missing fill price. The monitor reads
the in-progress bar from a live Alpaca IEX query; `candles` is written later by
candle_backfill.py from a different consolidation. 8 of 173 fills (4.6%) sit
outside their own backfilled bar's OHLC range, and no candle-based replay can
reproduce them because the price it filled at is not in the candle table.

What actually closes it is recording THE BAR THE MONITOR OBSERVED. With that,
replay can reconcile against the series the decision was made on. The diff
below therefore adds the observed reference bar alongside the fill fields.

Properties: additive columns only, all nullable, no behavioural change, no
effect on what the system trades, no change to any exit decision. Existing rows
keep NULL. SQLite ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN is non-rewriting.

Migration (run once, offline, on a backed-up DB):

    ALTER TABLE trades ADD COLUMN fill_price REAL;
    ALTER TABLE trades ADD COLUMN fill_ts DATETIME;
    ALTER TABLE trades ADD COLUMN fill_source TEXT;
    ALTER TABLE trades ADD COLUMN obs_bar_ts DATETIME;
    ALTER TABLE trades ADD COLUMN obs_bar_open REAL;
    ALTER TABLE trades ADD COLUMN obs_bar_high REAL;
    ALTER TABLE trades ADD COLUMN obs_bar_low REAL;
    ALTER TABLE trades ADD COLUMN obs_bar_close REAL;


