Risks reviewed
--------------
- `_close_position` gains two keyword args with defaults, so the existing
  prediction-cycle call site at trading_engine.py:282 is unaffected and keeps
  recording fill_source="prediction_cycle".
- `df.iloc[-1]` on a limit=2 fetch is the in-progress bar. That is the point:
  it is what the decision was taken on. It is recorded, not acted on.
- If get_ohlcv returns a frame without OHLC columns the dict build raises
  inside the existing per-symbol try/except, which already logs and continues
  to the next symbol. Worth confirming against data_fetcher before applying.
- No column is read by any live code path. Writes only.

What this does NOT fix
----------------------
Retrospective Pattern C. The 8 historical out-of-bar fills stay unmodelable;
this only stops new ones from being unexplainable. Nor does it address the
second bias mechanism found in Task 5 (overshoot/bar-range decoupling), which
is a harness-side fix.
